  "label": "Meme depicting a man's expression juxtaposed with text about a fatal car accident",
  "description": "The scene is composed of a man (actor Mike Myers) with a stern, unimpressed facial expression, positioned centrally in the foreground. Overlaid on the image are two lines of white text: 'there was a 4 car pile-up in mexico' at the top and 'today 93 people died' at the bottom. The background is a dark promotional event backdrop with partial text visible. The scene's composition uses the man's expression as a visual punchline to mock the tragic event described in the text, creating a juxtaposition between the trivialized reaction and the serious consequence.",
